  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Before patterns and problems, let's understand&nbsp;<strong>what a trie actually is</strong>&nbsp;and why it exists.",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-the-problem-it-solves",
      "title": "1. The Problem It Solves",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Say you have a dictionary of words and you need to:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Check if a word exists",
            "Find all words starting with a prefix",
            "Autocomplete a partially typed word"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461041-618019871.png\" alt=\"mermaid-diagram-105.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Using a hash set:</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Search word → O(L) (L = word length) → fine<br>",
            "Find by prefix → O(n × L) → scan every word → slow<br>",
            "Autocomplete → O(n × L) → scan every word → slow<br>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A trie solves prefix-based operations in&nbsp;<strong>O(L)</strong>&nbsp;only depends on prefix length, not number of words",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-what-is-a-trie",
      "title": "2. What is a Trie?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A trie is a tree where each&nbsp;<strong>node represents a single character</strong>. Words are formed by following paths from the root downward.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Words:&nbsp;<code>[\"cat\", \"car\", \"card\", \"care\", \"bat\"]</code>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Each word is broken into characters and stored&nbsp;<strong>one letter at a time</strong>.<br>Common prefixes share the same path&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "for example,&nbsp;<code>cat</code>,&nbsp;<code>car</code>,&nbsp;<code>card</code>,&nbsp;<code>care</code>&nbsp;all share&nbsp;<strong>c → a</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "From there, the paths split:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<code>cat</code>&nbsp;ends at&nbsp;<strong>t</strong>",
            "<code>car</code>&nbsp;continues to&nbsp;<strong>r</strong>, and then splits into&nbsp;<strong>d (card)</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>e (care)</strong>",
            "<code>bat</code>&nbsp;starts separately from&nbsp;<strong>b → a → t</strong>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b><img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461042-205483974.png\" alt=\"mermaid-diagram-106.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\"></b>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">So instead of storing full words, trie stores&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">paths of characters</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">, sharing common prefixes to save time and space&nbsp;</span><br></b>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every path from root to a marked node spells out a complete word.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The name \"trie\" comes from re<strong>trie</strong>val.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3-structure-of-a-trie-node",
      "title": "3. Structure of a Trie Node",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461042-742435942.png\" alt=\"mermaid-diagram-107.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Each node needs two things:</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Children</strong>&nbsp;→ links to next characters (like a map or array of size 26 for a–z)",
            "<strong>End flag</strong>&nbsp;→ tells if a complete word ends at this node&nbsp;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "class TrieNode {\n    TrieNode[] children;\n    boolean isEnd;\n\n    TrieNode() {\n        children = new TrieNode[26];   // one slot per letter a-z\n        isEnd = false;\n    }\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Visually, each node stores&nbsp;<strong>links to next characters</strong>&nbsp;and a flag to mark word ending.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461042-784696014.png\" alt=\"mermaid-diagram-108.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Node for&nbsp;</span><code style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">'a'</code><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">:</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "children → array/map of next possible characters (some are null, some point to nodes)",
            "example:&nbsp;<code>children['c'] → Node</code>&nbsp;means there is a path from&nbsp;<code>'a'</code>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<code>'c'</code>",
            "all other missing characters →&nbsp;<code>null</code>",
            "isEnd = false → no word ends at this node"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So each node just says: “where can I go next?” and “does a word end here?”",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4-how-words-are-stored",
      "title": "4. How Words Are Stored",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Each character maps to an index:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461042-184561533.png\" alt=\"mermaid-diagram-111.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">index = character - 'a'</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Inserting \"cat\":",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Start from the root node.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Character&nbsp;<code>'c'</code></strong>Index =&nbsp;<code>'c' - 'a' = 2</code><code>root.children[2]</code>&nbsp;does not exist →&nbsp;<strong>create new node</strong>",
            "<strong>Character&nbsp;<code>'a'</code></strong>Index =&nbsp;<code>'a' - 'a' = 0</code><code>children[2].children[0]</code>&nbsp;does not exist →&nbsp;<strong>create new node</strong>",
            "<strong>Character&nbsp;<code>'t'</code></strong>Index =&nbsp;<code>'t' - 'a' = 19</code><code>children[0].children[19]</code>&nbsp;does not exist →&nbsp;<strong>create new node</strong>",
            "<strong>Mark End of Word&nbsp;</strong>Mark the node corresponding to&nbsp;<code>'t'</code>&nbsp;as:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "isEnd = true",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461042-446878145.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Path: root → c → a → t*</strong><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Inserting<code>\"car\"</code>into the Trie (after<code>\"cat\"</code>):",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Start from the root node.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "<strong>Character&nbsp;<code>'c'</code></strong>Index =&nbsp;<code>2</code><code>root.children[2]</code>&nbsp;<strong>already exists</strong>&nbsp;→ move to that node",
            "<strong>Character&nbsp;<code>'a'</code></strong>Index =&nbsp;<code>0</code><code>children[2].children[0]</code>&nbsp;<strong>already exists</strong>&nbsp;→ move to that node",
            "<strong>Character&nbsp;<code>'r'</code></strong>Index =&nbsp;<code>17</code><code>children[0].children[17]</code>&nbsp;<strong>does not exist</strong>&nbsp;→&nbsp;<strong>create new node</strong>",
            "<strong>Mark End of Word</strong>Mark&nbsp;<code>'r'</code>&nbsp;node:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "isEnd = true",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461043-744245278.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We are&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">storing words character by character in a tree structure (trie)</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;instead of storing whole words separately.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "While inserting a word, we start from the root and move through each character. If a node for that character already exists, we reuse it; otherwise, we create a new node.&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "At the last character, we mark&nbsp;isEnd = true&nbsp;to indicate a complete word.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "So overall, we are building shared paths for common prefixes, avoiding duplication and making prefix operations fast&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5-core-operations",
      "title": "5. Core Operations",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "1. Insert",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Walk through the trie character by character. Move if path exists, otherwise create it. Mark end at the last character.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "<strong>Insert \"dog\":</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>S</strong>tart at root",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "'d' → root.children[3] → move/create 'd'<br>'o' → children[3].children[14] → move/create 'o'<br>'g' → children[14].children[6] → move/create 'g'<br>mark isEnd = true",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Path: root → d → o → g*&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461802-302600921.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We are&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">adding the word into the trie one character at a time</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Starting from the root, for each character (d → o → g), we either follow the existing path or create a new node if it doesn’t exist. At the last character, we mark&nbsp;isEnd = true&nbsp;to show that a complete word ends here.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "So basically, we are building a path for the word and storing it efficiently, sharing nodes if prefixes already exist&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\"></strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "void insert(String word) {\n    TrieNode curr = root;\n\n    for (char ch : word.toCharArray()) {\n        int idx = ch - 'a';\n\n        if (curr.children[idx] == null) {\n            curr.children[idx] = new TrieNode();   // create if missing\n        }\n\n        curr = curr.children[idx];   // move down\n    }\n\n    curr.isEnd = true;   // mark end of word\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">Time:&nbsp;<strong>O(L):&nbsp;</strong>L is word length</strong><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "2. Search",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Walk character by character. If any character is missing → word doesn’t exist. At the end, check&nbsp;isEnd.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Search</b> \"car\":<br>root → c → a → r → isEnd = true → found ✓",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Search</b> \"ca\":<br>root → c → a → isEnd = false → not a complete word ✗",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Search</b> \"cap\":<br>root → c → a → p (missing) → not found ✗&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461803-236185409.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We are&nbsp;</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">checking if a word exists in the trie by following its path</span><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Starting from the root, we move character by character (c → a → r). If at any point a character path is missing, the word doesn’t exist. If we reach the end, we check&nbsp;<strong>isEnd</strong>&nbsp;only if it’s true, the word is valid.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "So we are basically verifying: “Does this exact path exist, and does a word end here?”&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "boolean search(String word) {\n    TrieNode curr = root;\n\n    for (char ch : word.toCharArray()) {\n        int idx = ch - 'a';\n\n        if (curr.children[idx] == null) return false;   // path broken\n\n        curr = curr.children[idx];\n    }\n\n    return curr.isEnd;   // must be marked as a complete word\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Time: O(L)</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "3. Starts With (Prefix Search)",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Same as search, but you don’t check&nbsp;<strong>isEnd</strong>. Just verify the path exists.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Prefix</b> \"ca\":<br>root → c → a → path exists → true ✓",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Prefix</b> \"do\":<br>root → d → o → path exists → true ✓",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<b>Prefix</b> \"dx\":<br>root → d → x (missing) → false ✗",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785406461803-856764634.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">We are&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">checking if any word starts with a given prefix</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">.</span><br>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Starting from the root, we follow each character of the prefix (like c → a). If the full path exists, it means some word uses this prefix, so return&nbsp;<code>true</code>. We don’t care if a word ends here (no need to check isEnd).",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "So we are just verifying: “Does this prefix path exist in the trie?”&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "boolean startsWith(String prefix) {\n    TrieNode curr = root;\n\n    for (char ch : prefix.toCharArray()) {\n        int idx = ch - 'a';\n\n        if (curr.children[idx] == null) return false;\n\n        curr = curr.children[idx];\n    }\n\n    return true;   // path exists, don't care about isEnd\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<strong>Time: O(L)</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading4",
          "text": "Full Trie Class",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "class Trie {\n    TrieNode root;\n\n    Trie() {\n        root = new TrieNode();\n    }\n\n    void insert(String word) {\n        TrieNode curr = root;\n        for (char ch : word.toCharArray()) {\n            int idx = ch - 'a';\n            if (curr.children[idx] == null)\n                curr.children[idx] = new TrieNode();\n            curr = curr.children[idx];\n        }\n        curr.isEnd = true;\n    }\n\n    boolean search(String word) {\n        TrieNode curr = root;\n        for (char ch : word.toCharArray()) {\n            int idx = ch - 'a';\n            if (curr.children[idx] == null) return false;\n            curr = curr.children[idx];\n        }\n        return curr.isEnd;\n    }\n\n    boolean startsWith(String prefix) {\n        TrieNode curr = root;\n        for (char ch : prefix.toCharArray()) {\n            int idx = ch - 'a';\n            if (curr.children[idx] == null) return false;\n            curr = curr.children[idx];\n        }\n        return true;\n    }\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
