      "blocks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "6-memory-layout",
      "title": "6. Memory Layout",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One important thing tries can use a lot of memory.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Each node stores an array of&nbsp;<strong>26 pointers</strong>, even if most are&nbsp;<code>null</code>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For&nbsp;<strong>example</strong>:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1000 words × average 5 characters → about 5000 nodes",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Each node → 26 pointers → 26 × 8 bytes = 208 bytes",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Total memory → 5000 × 208 ≈&nbsp;<strong>1 MB for just 1000 words</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "So tries are fast, but they trade speed for higher memory usage&nbsp;",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "items": [],
          "codes": {
            "javascript": "class TrieNode {\n    Map<Character, TrieNode> children = new HashMap<>();\n    boolean isEnd = false;\n}"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Instead of storing all 26 possible children, we store&nbsp;<strong>only the characters that actually exist</strong>&nbsp;(using a map/dictionary).",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "7-trie-vs-hash-map",
      "title": "7. Trie vs Hash Map",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Trie is best when problems involve&nbsp;<strong>prefix search, autocomplete, or shared prefixes</strong>, because it stores common paths once and lets you find results quickly",
          "items": []
        },
        {
